    "result_text": "That's a JaCoCo coverage exclusion, not a test filter. `AcceptanceTest` is the only concrete test class, so the full suite is that one test, and it's green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `checkDigit` as a derived, read-only field equal to the Luhn check digit computed over the digits of the owner's `customerCode`, following the existing pattern for other derived fields (`membershipLevel`, `contactPreference`, `identityKey`).\n\nTwo changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `checkDigit` property (integer 0\u20139, `readOnly`) to the `Owner` schema, right after `customerCode`. The build generates `OwnerDto` from this spec, and MapStruct auto-maps it from a matching getter.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added `getCheckDigit()`, which computes the Luhn check digit over the digits in `customerCode` (non-digits ignored, rightmost digit doubled), replicating the exact algorithm the acceptance test uses in `luhn(...)`. It returns `null` when there's no customer code.\n\nThe endpoint now returns `checkDigit` in the `GET /api/owners/{id}` response. The full test suite passes: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
